0 Small winch and pulley displays show cord wound around shafts, lowered to hooks and looped over wheels.
0 Name: STRING_HOSE-Constraints.ldr
0 Author: Willy Tschager
0 Unofficial Model
0 // Scene: A blue cord leaves a reel and passes around a large hanging hook block. Beside it, a yellow line descends from a wound shaft to a smaller hook, and another shaft carries a short brown winding.
0 // Rigid construction: The rigid pieces include a 32012 reel, 4185 sheaves, a large 30 hook, a 3127 plate-mounted hook and short axles. Other samples compare closed and open cord routes.
0 // Build lesson: A crane needs recognizable rope hardware: drum, sheave, hook block and supports. Follow the continuous line through those parts before designing the surrounding boom.
0 // Reuse: The display leaves shafts and upper supports unframed; rope anchoring, a brake and mechanical advantage remain unproven. The supplied synthesis contains only the first three studies; the three later STRING_BAND routes are present only in these constraints.
0 ROTATION CENTER 0 0 0 1 "Custom" 
0 ROTATION CONFIG 0 0
